  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "These are issues primarily affected by people with slow internet connections.\n\n1. Blocking avatars by default does not abort downloading: \nWhen I join a world, peoples avatars start downloading, and when I then change the setting to \"block avatars by default\", the avatars are hidden initially, but the downloads continue, and worse: once the download of an avatar has been finished it actually reappears despite the \"block avatars\" setting. I have to uncheck and recheck the setting to make it disappear, but this potentially causes other avatars of other users, that have been properly blocked, to start downloading instead.\n\nI believe this issue even exists on users I blocked in the middle of downloading.\n\n2. When I join a world and the avatars start downloading. If I then realize I'm not interested in staying in that world (e.g. no one speaks english or some other reason) and switch to another world, the avatars of that previous world still download in the background. After joining the second world, the avatars often don't start downloading immediately but only get scheduled. So I have to either wait for the \"background avatars\" to finish or restart my client.\n\nSometimes this even happens when I try to join a world I haven't been to yet. The world does not start downloading, probably because there are still avatars downloading in the background. A restart of the client usually \"fixes\" that.\n\n3. Joining a world i haven't been to yet, starts the download. Returning to home mid-download however, does not abort the download as well. The world still downloads in the background.\n\nI usually use this as a \"feature\" though. When I want to join a world, I usually just join it to start the download, then return home mid-download, rejoin my friends I have been with earlier (in a world I already have cached), and after a couple minutes I can join the world that has now been fully downloading without having to wait.\n\n---\n\nThe avatar thingie is a problematic I believe. It would be great though, if there is a proper way to download a world, without having to leave the current world, so I can still stay with my friends.\n\n---\n\nEdit: Another thing I forgot to mention: When a user switches to an avatar and it starts downloading, and afterwards he switches to another avatar mid-download, then the download progress bar (the yellow thing) blinks back and forth between to progresses, because there are two downloads happening.\n\nAlso, if the second avatar finishes downloading before the first one, the user does appear with the second avatar, and the progress bar disappears, even though the first avatar is still downloading. Once the first avatar finishes downloading however, the user suddenly changes to that avatar instead, even though he should have the second one. I usually have to either toggle the \"block avatars by default\" to see the correct avatar, or block and unblock the user to see it properly.",
